{"availability":"available","full":"vladocar/ramd.js","name":"ramd.js","description":"ramd.js JavaScript library for making web applications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":62,"forks":4,"created":"2018-07-14T09:51:36Z","updated":"2018-07-16T15:21:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["crud","crud-application","javascript","library","webapp"],"demo":"https://vladocar.github.io/ramd.js/simple-todo.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T19:06:59.510Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T19:06:59.510Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T19:06:59.510Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:01:25.302Z","stars":62,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:03:37.407Z","stars":62,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-16T19:06:59.510Z","stars":62,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Minimal standalone JS library for building web applications.","RAMD or Render - Add - Modify - Delete is minimal 0.65 kb library for making simple list projects. Everything is based on the \"simplified virtual DOM\" that is basically JavaScript Object listing the essential element properties. This Object acts like internal DB that can be stored locally or send to the server. The importance of the \"virtualdom\" vs DOM is not about the speed but rather ease of use and storage.","The Object method \"1531563018024-9718829aa677\" is Timestamp - Random Number. You can use the Timestamp to determine when the element was added."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vladocar/ramd.js/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"8623c23e4deaadc5a59e043254301c13c051bbeac998636406730dab4a67c657","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:25.466Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:25.466Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Minimal standalone JS library for building web applications.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vladocar/ramd.js/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8623c23e